    slide('Extension','Extension bridge · infinite geometric series','content','Optional enrichment — not assessed as core SL 1.3 content',`<div class="gs-two"><div class="gs-key"><b>CONVERGENCE PREVIEW</b><p>If \\(|r|<1\\), then \\(r^n\\to0\\) and the finite sums approach</p><div class="gs-big-math">\\[S_{\\infty}=\\frac{u_1}{1-r}\\]</div><p>If \\(|r|\\geq1\\), the infinite series does not converge to a finite sum.</p></div><div class="gs-extension-visual"><div><span>partial sums</span><b>\\(S_1,S_2,S_3,\\ldots\\)</b></div><i>approach</i><div><span>finite limit</span><b>\\(S_{\\infty}\\)</b></div><p>Example: \\(1+1/2+1/4+\\cdots=2\\).</p></div></div><div class="gs-warning"><b>Scope label:</b> this screen is a conceptual bridge to later or higher-level work. The lesson’s core Practice Studio, quiz and IB tasks assess finite geometric sequences and series.</div>`)
